.TH "smtool" "1" "2025-08-21" "1.0.0-beta2" "SpectMorph Manual"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
smtool - tool to show/change SpectMorph data from .sm/.smset files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]smtool\f[R] \f[I]|\f[R] \f[I]\f[R] [ \f[I]\f[R] ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]smtool\f[R] is a general purpose program that can perform
operations on .sm/.smset files.
Some of the operations extract data (like \f[B]size\f[R]), others modify
data (like \f[B]auto-tune\f[R]).
If a .smset file is given as argument, the operation is performed on the
individual .sm files that are contained in the .smset file.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\f[B]smtool\f[R] options depend on the command used, the command
specific arguments are listed below.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]volume\f[R] \f[I]\f[R]
Compute average energy of the audio data around \f[I]\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]fundamental-freq\f[R]
Output fundamental frequency of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]mix-freq\f[R]
Output mixing frequency (sample rate) of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]zero-values-at-start\f[R]
Output zero-values-at-start property of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]attack\f[R]
Output attack parameters of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]size\f[R]
Output overview of the size in bytes of the different parts of the audio
data.
.TP
\f[B]loop-params\f[R]
Output loop parameters of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]noise-params\f[R] \f[I]\f[R]
Output noise component of a frame of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]frame\f[R] \f[I]\f[R]
Show original samples and reconstructed samples for one frame of the
audio data.
.TP
\f[B]frame-params\f[R] \f[I]\f[R]
Show the freqencies/magnitudes of one frame of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]total-noise\f[R]
Sum up all noise parameters of all frames of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]nan-test\f[R]
Check all frame data contents for NaNs.
.TP
\f[B]original-samples\f[R]
Show original samples of the audio data.
.TP
\f[B]freq\f[R] \f[I]\f[R] \f[I]\f[R]
Show all frequency entries of the audio data in the specified range.
.TP
\f[B]spectrum\f[R] \f[I]\f[R]
Compare original and reconstructed spectrum for a given frame.
.TP
\f[B]auto-loop\f[R] \f[I]\f[R]
Set a one frame loop that starts and ends at the same point (given by
\f[I]\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]tail-loop\f[R]
Loop audio data at the end using a one frame loop.
.TP
\f[B]auto-tune\f[R]
Tune instrument using the (40%..60%) data to extract the actual
frequency.
.TP
\f[B]tune-all-frames\f[R]
Tune each frame of the instrument.
This will discard minimal changes in frequency which are normal for most
instruments, so it might sound artificial.
.TP
\f[B]auto-volume\f[R] \f[I]\f[R]
Normalize audio volume, using the volume around \f[I]\f[R] as reference.
.TP
\f[B]auto-volume-from-loop\f[R]
Normalize audio volume, using the volume of the looped part as
reference.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
smenc.1, smplay.1
